\begin{notn}\label{modT}
Fix a listing $\set{\vp_i\mid i\in\omega}$ of all atomic $(\mc L\cup\omega)$-sentences, where elements of $\omega$ are viewed as constants. We identify any $\mc L$-structure $\mc A$ with domain $\omega$ with its atomic diagram $\mc D(\mc A)\in2^\omega$, i.e. $\mc D(\mc A)(i)=1$ if $\mc A\sat\vp_i$ and 0 otherwise.

The set $\Mod(T)$ of an $\mc L$-theory $T$ is the set of all countable models of $T$.

\end{notn}

