By a density argument on $u$, one concludes that $M^{\frac{s}{2}}K_x=M^{-\frac{s}{2}}\gamma_N\big(G_1(x,\cdot)\big)$ a.e. on $\partial\Omega$. Therefore, for any $x,y\in\Omega$,
\[
K_s(x,y)=\langle M^{\frac{s}{2}}K_x,\,M^{\frac{s}{2}}K_y\rangle_{L^2(\partial\Omega)}
=\big\langle M^{-\frac{s}{2}}\gamma_N\big(G_1(x,\cdot)\big),\,M^{-\frac{s}{2}}\gamma_N\big(G_1(y,\cdot)\big)\big\rangle_{L^2(\partial\Omega)},
