Such solutions are regarded as the “particle-like solutions” and hence attract much attention. 
For spinors of such form and for~$F$ invariant under rotations ( i.e. ~$F(e^{i\theta}\Psi)=F(\Psi)$),~\eqref{eq:4D nonlinear Dirac} is transformed into
\begin{align}
 i\gamma^k\p_k\psi + a\gamma^0\psi-m\psi +\gamma^0\nabla F(\psi)=0.
\end{align}
Equivalently, we are led to consider the equation
\begin{align}\label{eq:NDE-spatial}\tag{*}
 -i\gamma^0 \gamma^k\p_k \psi + m\gamma^0\psi -a\psi-\nabla F(\psi)=0.
\end{align}
