\end{align}
where~$\Gamma\subset \mathbb{R}^3$ is a 3-dimensional lattice.
They are referred as the standing periodic waves for~\eqref{eq:4D nonlinear Dirac}.

In quantum fields theory it is often required that the Hamiltonian has some symmetry, and the periodicity is thus frequently imposed. 
In one-dimensional dynamics this is usually the case. 
According to the features of the particle system, sometimes it is require that the nonlinearity has spatial periodicity, which is not the case here since our~$F$ has no explicit dependence on the space variable~$x$. 
