For any fixed parameter $k\in\mathbb{N}$, we say that a metric measure space $(X,\mathrm{d},\mathfrak m)$ admits the $L^2$-CKN inequalities (with parameter $k$) if there exists a constant $C(k)>0$ such that, for all
\[
u\in \mathrm{Lip}_b(X,\mathrm{d}) := \{ v:\ v \text{ is Lipschitz with bounded support}\},
\]
