\widetilde{v_H^\varepsilon}(m)
=
d f_1^\varepsilon\bigl((f_1^\varepsilon)^{-1}(m)\bigr)
\Bigl[v_H^{\omega_0+\varepsilon_1,\sigma_0+\varepsilon_2}\bigl((f_1^\varepsilon)^{-1}(m)\bigr)\Bigr],
\end{align}
for all $m\in \mathrm{dom}(\mathbf{L})$ with sufficiently small $\|m\|_{X^2}$. Using \eqref{newvH}, a straightforward but tedious computation
