\label{thm 1}
Let $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^m$ be a bounded  Lipschitz domain symmetric about the origin. Suppose $h(r)\in C^2([0, +\infty))$ satisfies  $h'(r)\ge 0$ and $h''(r)\ge 0$ for $r\in (0, +\infty)$. Let  $B \subset \mathbb{R}^m$  be the  origin-centered  round ball with the same $\gamma_h$-volume as $\Omega$, namely $ \int_{\Omega} e^{h(|x|)}\, dx= \int_{B} e^{h(|x|)}\, dx$. Denote by $\sigma_1(B; \gamma_h)$ the first nonzero Steklov eigenvalue of \eqref{eq 1.4} on $B$, and $\l_{2,\alpha}(\Omega; \gamma_h)$ the second Robin eigenvalue of \eqref{eq 1.1} on $\Omega$.  If  $\alpha \in [-\sigma_1(B; \gamma_h), 0]$, then 
\begin{align}\label{eq 1.6}
\l_{2,\alpha}(\Omega; \gamma_h) \le \l_{2,\alpha}(B; \gamma_h).
\end{align}
Equality holds  if and only if 
$\Omega=B$.

