The post-theorem text does not give a step-by-step proof, but it indicates the strategy in a special case (when $Y$ is the rational elliptic surface mirror to $\mathbb{P}^2$ and $D$ is a singular fiber “consisting of a cycle of nine copies of $\mathbb{P}^1$”). The argument “relies on the correspondence between log Gromov–Witten invariants of $(Y,D)$ and Vafa--Witten invariants of $\mathbb{P}^2$, established in joint work with Bousseau \cite[Theorem 4.1]{ABquiverscurves}.” The paper’s stated approach is to “transport this anticipated mock modularity from Vafa–Witten theory to the setting of log Gromov–Witten theory for elliptic fibrations”.

We first prove the following theorem.
\begin{theorem}
\label{thm:logGW/VW generating}
    For any $r \in \ZZ_{\geq 0}$ and $c_1 \in \ZZ$ with $-1 < \frac{c_1}{r} \leq 0$, the log Gromov--Witten generating series for $(Y,D)$ and the Vafa--Witten generating series for $\PP^2$, given in Equations \eqref{Eq:log GW generating} and \eqref{eq: vw generating} respectively are equal:
   \[ h^{GW}_{r,c_1}(\tau) = h^{VW}_{r,c_1}(\tau) \, . \]
\end{theorem}

Consequently, we obtain the following corollary.
\begin{corollary}
\label{cor:proof of mock log}
Let $(Y,D)$ be the rational elliptic surface mirror to $\PP^2$ as in \S\ref{sec:rational elliptic}.
For any $1 \leq r \leq 3$, the vector $(h^{GW}_{r,c_1}(\tau))_{-r< c_1 \leq 0}$, with components the log Gromov--Witten generating series of $(Y,D)$ given in \eqref{Eq:log GW generating}, is a vector-valued mock modular form of weight $-\frac{3}{2}$ and depth $r$.
\end{corollary}

This deduction uses the expected/known mock modular behavior of the Vafa--Witten series for $\mathbb{P}^2$ (since $h^{2,0}(\mathbb{P}^2)=0$).

